      "content": "Understood. So it's more of a technicality of title and physical compliance than a nuisance issue. \n\nFollowing up on that: when these \"encroachments\" or \"unresolved boundary disputes\" are being presented during the administrative review, is there any specific way the city categorizes them based on how they've occurred? For instance, if an encroachment is seen as an \"intrusion\" or an \"unauthorized entry\" into the property's required buffer zones, does the code differentiate between accidental setbacks and more deliberate or problematic incursions that seem to intentionally infringe upon the parcel's boundaries? I want to know if there's a distinction in how they handle these types of territorial infringements.",
